<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Reaction Surface ~ the record

The projection bus speaks at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/vm-projection-bus`>> and the reaction graph at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/reaction-graph`>>. This record keeps how the reaction surface reached its shape.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-collapse`>>

!! The collapse

The reaction graph's yin-collapse slot read ''What shipped'' and told it so:

> `ReactionGraph` and `extractReactionBindings` reside in `reaction-graph.ts` (imported by `reaction-router.ts`). `ReactionEngine` class removed from `kumu-device.ts`. No inline `re.onChangeset()` call remains anywhere.
>
> TS irreducible layer carries only: `MemeSyncAdaptor` + `LarTiddlerStore` + `VesselIslandPool` + Keyhive.

No class named `MemeSyncAdaptor` stands; the wiki shore (`IslandAdaptor`) holds that place. The dispatch-modes slot read `fireRace` / `fireRush` as ''reserved for competitive dispatch (future: multi-realm routing)''; `ReactionGraph` implements `fireSync` alone. The slot read that `reaction-router.ts` fires `IslandMsg_Event`; the router fires `tm-verse-event` and the island kernel posts the island message.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/first-design-reading`>>

!! The bus's first design reading

The projection bus first named its consumer `ReactionEngine`, its interface as ''defined in `@lararium/mesh`'', and its caller as ''VmPool or LarariumShell''. The consumer shape stands inline on `onVerseEvent` in `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-vm.ts`; the island kernel registers through it; no `VmPool` or `LarariumShell` class stands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/section-stamps`>>

!! Section stamps

Both memes' Scope-1 sections carried the stamp ''[surgical 2026-07-03]'', the day the two-scopes ruling seated them.

<<~/ahu>>

